## Context

`tickets/AGENTS.md` states that on GitHub, `tickets/erg-github` adds a
`verify` check failing a PR that references a still-open ticket. No such
helper exists in this repo (confirmed twice during ticket 0262's execution
and its review, 2026-07-11): CI's `validate-tickets` job runs only
`erg check tickets/`. The sentence misleads agents into designing around a
boundary that is not there — 0262's original plan assumed it.

Note: this text comes from the global `~/.claude/tickets/AGENTS.md`, which
projects mirror; check whether the fix belongs in the shared source, the
git-erg adopter template, or both.

## Actions

1. Decide: ship the helper (from the git-erg project, if it exists there),
   or correct the sentence to describe what actually runs.
2. Apply in the canonical source and re-sync mirrors as appropriate.

## Exit criteria

- `tickets/AGENTS.md` describes only checks that actually run on this repo,
  or the described helper exists and runs in CI.
